# Binary files, so that Git never applies text conversion to them. Phobos ships a
# compiled preload library in version control; a Git that normalised it would corrupt it.
*.so       binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.tar      binary
*.gz       binary
*.tgz      binary
*.zip      binary
*.7z       binary

# Not exported in an archive.
.gitattributes export-ignore
.gitignore     export-ignore

# NOTE, deliberately absent: a `* text=auto eol=lf` line.
#
# Several files in this repository are stored with CRLF line endings. A blanket
# normalisation rule here would silently rewrite them all. A CRLF Dockerfile is worth
# fixing, because a trailing carriage return ends up inside the RUN command, but that is a
# behaviour change that needs a Docker build to verify and belongs in its own pull request
# rather than in a repository hygiene change. Tracked in ls1intum/phobos#15.
#
# This comment used to list the affected files by name and had gone stale: it named
# ld_preloader/netblocker.c, which is stored with LF. Ask Git instead of trusting a list
# that nothing keeps in step:
#
#     git ls-files --eol | grep crlf
#
# At the time of writing that reports eight files, under core/, docker/run_phase,
# ld_preloader/, security_config/, squid/ and var/tmp.
